Fvwm release 0.95 (source and binaries) has been uploaded to sunsite,
as file /pub/Linux/X11/window-managers/fvwm-0.95-source.tar.z and
/pub/Linux/X11/window-managers/fvwm-0.95-binaries.tar.z.

Fvwm is a light-weight window manager which provides a simple virtual
desktop, a 3-D look for windows decorations, and color icons.

Memory consumption for Fvwm is about 1/2 to 1/3 that of twm.
Fvwm is targeted at machines with too little memory, and at laptops
on which mouse usage may be awkward. All window manager functions
can be performed (conveniently) without a mouse.

In this release we have the following one new features:
1. You can now switch to another window manager by using the restart function
   for example
	Restart "Switch to Twm" twm
   this means that you need to update your .fvwmrc files:
	    Was				    Should Be
       ---------------------------------------------------------
	Restart "Restart Fvwm"      Restart "Restart Fvwm"  fvwm

Bug Fixes:
1. Fixed some occasional crashes.
2. Fixed the problem of not being able to bind keyboard keys to actions
   in the root window.
3. Emacs-19 icons, when iconified using ^z, should now be visible
4. After killing an application which started before fvwm started, we
   used to get zombies. This has been fixed. (Twm has the zombie
   problem too).
5. Menu title entries are fixed up a bit.
6. Windows which change their colormaps after they appear on the screen
   are now handled properly.


New bugs:
As usual, I have attempted to include at least one new bug. Since I uploaded
the releases to sunsite several days ago, and some people already have it, I 
will just append the patch to this message. If you get the binaries, rest
assured that the bug only causes hand-placed windows to jump
around during re-start operations. No big deal.


