I just uploaded the latest version of CircleMUD (version 2.10) to
tsx-11.mit.edu.  Version 2.10 runs under Linux, which is why I'm
posting to this newsgroup.

The distribution has sources, but no binaries.  If there is any need,
I can upload binaries as well, but compiling is very easy ... all you
have to do is make one change to the Makefile to activate Linux
support and then type 'make all'.

I just realized that the running and maintenance scripts are broken under
Linux because Linux doesn't have csh, but the scripts aren't vital to
the MUD's operation and can be easily ported to bash if you want to use
them anyway.

Files uploaded:

circle-2.10.tar.Z   -  CircleMUD 2.10 distribution, tarred and compressed.
circle-2.10-README  -  Text file describing Circle's features.

