Hi! Another release. No big changes, just to keep up-to-date with the
latest kernel release.

This is release 0.4 of atdisk2 patch for Linux 0.99.10 & 0.99.11 (also
work with 0.99.11+Jul22_ALPHA). The patch in this package enables
Linux to use a second AT-type (16-bit) hard disk controller with 2
drives maximum attached to it.

The files:

atdisk2-0.4.note --- a short note about the package
atdisk2-0.4.tgz  --- a gzipped tar file of the package

should appear in the following sites soon:

tsx-11.mit.edu:pub/linux/BETA/atdisk
nic.funet.fi:pub/OS/Linux/BETA/atdisk
sunsite.unc.edu:pub/Linux/kernel/misc-patches

[If the files haven't appeared in any of the directories above, they
can be found in sunsite.unc.edu:pub/Linux/Incoming.]

Have fun with it!

